VLHE - Credits and References
=============================

VLHE contains no code from the projects below. They were studied
for their design, documentation or behaviour, and all VLHE code was
written independently. Thanks to their authors.


Projects studied
----------------

CDEmu / virtualcd 0.3
  Robert Penz, 2002
  https://cdemu.sourceforge.io/
  (as it was then: https://web.archive.org/web/20031213165957/http://cdemu.sourceforge.net/)
  Licence: GPL-2.0
  Informed: the virtual CD-ROM design in vdisc. "virtualcd" is the
  name it had before the rename to CDEmu.

CD+G Deck
  Isaac Brodsky, 2020
  https://github.com/isaacbrodsky/cdgdeck
  Licence: BSD-3-Clause
  Informed: two findings that changed our decoder. BORDER_PRESET
  must set a colour and write no pixels - filling the border
  destroys artwork a later scroll brings into view, which is why
  VLC cannot play "Jimi Hendrix - Smash Hits" - and the geometry of
  the border mask, one tile on every side. Its rotateH/rotateV were
  also transcribed into a test (tests/cdgcmp/scrollcmp.c) to check
  our coarse scroll against: 124 scrolls on that disc, no
  difference.

FreeBSD sound/pcm (stable/13)
  https://cgit.freebsd.org/src/tree/sys/dev/sound/pcm?h=stable/13
  Licence: BSD-2-Clause
  Informed: how a software audio layer sits between applications
  and a hardware driver - the architecture behind vsound's mixer.

GTK+ 1.2
  https://download.gnome.org/sources/gtk+/1.2/
  Licence: LGPL-2.0
  Informed: GdkRGB's indexed-image path, used to plan the CD+G
  paint path in vsound. Reading gdkrgb.c is what showed that its
  indexed converter is specialised only at 8bpp and takes two
  passes at 15/16/24/32, which is why the viewer writes its own
  pixels.

awesfx
  Takashi Iwai
  https://github.com/tiwai/awesfx
  Licence: GPL-2.0
  Informed: the SoundFont container format and both AWE
  attenuation curves, for vmidi's synth.

TiMidity++ 2.11.3
  https://timidity.sourceforge.net/
  Licence: GPL-2.0
  Informed: SoundFont loading and its volume curve.

FluidSynth
  https://www.fluidsynth.org/
  Licence: LGPL-2.1
  Informed: voice rendering - the filter, resampler and unit
  conversions.

QuakeForge 0.1.1, LxDoom 1.4.1
  https://www.quakeforge.net/
  https://web.archive.org/web/20001206030400/http://lxdoom.linuxgames.com/
  Licence: GPL-2.0
  Informed: how period games drive CD audio and MIDI, which is
  what vdisc and vmidi have to satisfy.


Specifications and documentation
--------------------------------

SoundFont 2.01 specification
  Informed: the SF2 reader in vmidi

CD+G Revealed, Jim Bumgardner
  http://jbum.com/cdg_revealed.html
  Informed: CD+G packet decoding (lib/cdg.c) - the subcode packet
  structure design/34 works from

<Wacom IV protocol notes>
  Informed: the serial protocol emulated by the tablet bridge

Wacom Tablet HOWTO v1.0.6, Stefan Runkel, March 2000
  Shipped by Corel in wacom-xdriver_1.0. Informed: the XF86Config
  XInput section, and it dates the USB decision this project began
  with.


Reference behaviour
-------------------

CD+G Deck (see above)
  Used as a reference player when comparing CD+G playback

karadeo.com CDG Karaoke Player
  https://karadeo.com/cdg-player
  Used as a second reference player, in a browser

KsCD (KDE 1.1)
  Corel's build, from kde-corel-source_1.1.1251.tgz
  Licence: GPL-2.0
  Reference for CD player behaviour: what a Play/Pause button does,
  and that a paused player keeps its time display where a stopped
  one blanks it.


